## Graphical Abstract
A highly efficient combi-metal organic frameworks (combi-MOF) of $\mathfrak{a}$ -amylase and glucoamylase was prepared for starch hydrolysis which exhibited excellent thermal and storage stability.
Highlights:
► Combi-MOF of $\mathfrak{a}$ -amylase and glucoamylase was prepared by co-precipitation method in one pot method.
$\blacktriangleright$ The prepared combi-MOF was analyzed and characterized by using FT-IR, XRD, TGA and SEM.
►Thermal stability of combi-MOF was improved in the temperature range of $55\mathrm{-}75^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ as compared to free.
Combi-MOF exhibited superb reusability and storage stability which make it industrial applicable.
$\blacktriangleright$ The starch hydrolytic activity of combi-MOF was tested for corn, rice, wheat and potato starch.
